From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: yodaliu <yodaliu@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 12:55:32 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 4/4] asoc: bengal: FiiO M21 audio routing

- PRI MI2S RX plays to the FiiO DAC (fiio_codec / fiio HiFi, CPU DAI
  fiio-snd-soc-dummy-dai); no WSA speaker amp on the RX DMA links.
- WSA MI2S back ends use the primary port; with qcom,mi2s-master the SoC drives
  the I2S clocks and MCLK_2 (24.576 MHz, 22.5792 MHz for 44.1 kHz rates) for the
  WSA/VA primary MI2S streams.
- qcom,wcd-disabled skips the WCD937x codec setup.
- qcom,msm-spk-ext-pa: external speaker amp enable GPIO, switched by the
  Ext_Spk_Switch mixer control.

Reconstructed from the stock FiiO M21 FW 1.1.0 machine_dlkm; the rebuilt
module matches it.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
